**Diagram to draw:** the outline of the body of a male mammal (e.g. a man, front view) with the glands shown in position and labelled:

- **Pituitary gland:** at the base of the brain, under the hypothalamus;
- **Thyroid gland:** in the neck, in front of the trachea (windpipe);
- **Parathyroid glands:** small glands at the back of the thyroid;
- **Adrenal glands:** one on top of each kidney;
- **Pancreas (islets of Langerhans):** below the stomach, close to the duodenum;
- **Testes:** in the scrotum, below the abdomen.

Show also the position of the kidneys and the stomach as reference organs. Use ruled label lines, a title (*Position of the endocrine glands in a male mammal*) and no arrow-heads on the label lines.
